	<application id="codes.tashif.paisa">
		<id>codes.tashif.paisa</id>
		<added>2026-07-25</added>
		<lastupdated>2026-11-16</lastupdated>
		<name>Paisa</name>
		<summary>Expense manager that reads bank SMS on your phone and keeps the ledger there</summary>
		<desc>Paisa is an expense manager that keeps your ledger on your phone. There is no account, no ads and no Paisa server.

Capture

* Bank SMS import. Parsers for about 140 Indian banks turn an alert into a transaction on the device. A bulk scan reads the inbox once and a live receiver catches new alerts
* The original SMS stays attached to the transaction it made
* Add with AI. Type or say what you spent, or attach a receipt, a screenshot or a PDF, then review the drafts before anything is saved
* Statement import for PDF, CSV and image statements, several at once
* Manual entry with Markdown descriptions

Review

* Merchant search, filters, and analytics by category and date range
* Monthly budgets per category
* Bank, cash, card and wallet accounts
* Bill splitting equally, by percentage, by amount or by item, with debts tracked per person

Make it yours

* Material You wallpaper colours or 31 fixed palettes, dark mode and AMOLED black
* High contrast, calmer motion and a floating navigation bar
* Home screen widgets for your balance and quick add
* Layouts for phones, foldables and tablets

Privacy

* SMS never leave the phone
* AI features stay off until you add your own key for an OpenAI compatible endpoint, Gemini or Anthropic
* App lock with a fingerprint, your face or the screen lock, and one tap to hide amounts
* Backups go to Google Drive, Nextcloud or a .paisa file, encrypted with AES-256-GCM when you set a password
* Export to CSV or PDF

Why it asks for permissions

* SMS, to read and receive bank alerts. SMS import is optional
* Microphone, for voice notes in Add with AI
* Network, for backup, sync and the AI endpoint you configure
* Biometrics, for app lock

The same app runs in a browser at https://paisa.tashif.codes
</desc>
